items.body:
### Reproduction steps

Launch Zed.
Select "Bypass Permissions" with Claude Agent pane.
Continue to see a bunch of confirmations (most scroll off the screen), asking for permission.

<img width="702" height="922" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2941a0ac-d25d-4dd7-ae8d-479ea05103af" />

So... much... clicking. :(

### Current vs. Expected behavior

Current behavior: I have to constantly monitor the AI agent pane and click the "Yes"/"No" prompts.

<img width="472" height="1215" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/327bbc62-bd21-4bfe-a289-3289742fea6a" />

<img width="229" height="606" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79fef9f5-23fe-4ca9-b2e9-fff740c66252" />

### Zed version and system specs

Zed: v1.18.1+stable.352.bebe92f469834a287f5a57ed78e8d51a918b8ada (Zed) 
OS: Windows 10.0.19045
Memory: 63.8 GiB
Architecture: x86_64
GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 || NVIDIA Corporation || 610.88 r610_85

